  "body": {
    "id": "thm:simultaneous-bands",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "Let \\(N=nm\\) and \\(d=|\\mathcal G_n|\\).  Under the predictable experiment class, polynomial family growth, and deterministic dense average-scale loadings, define\n\\[\n R_{g,\\alpha}=2B\\sqrt{\\frac{\\lVert g\\rVert_F^2}{q}\\log\\!\\frac{2d}{\\alpha}}\n +\\frac{2BC_\\infty}{qN}\\log\\!\\frac{2d}{\\alpha}.\n\\]\nThen, for every finite \\(n,m\\),\n\\[\n P\\!\\left(\\tau_g\\in[\\widehat\\tau_g-R_{g,\\alpha},\n \\widehat\\tau_g+R_{g,\\alpha}]\\text{ for every }g\\in\\mathcal G_n\\right)\n \\ge1-\\alpha.\n\\]\nUniformly in \\(g\\),\n\\[\n R_{g,\\alpha}=O\\!\\left(\n B\\sqrt{\\frac{\\log(2|\\mathcal G_n|/\\alpha)}{nmq}}\n +\\frac{B\\log(2|\\mathcal G_n|/\\alpha)}{qnm}\\right).\n\\]\nThus the simultaneous stochastic radius has the separate \\(\\sqrt{\\log|\\mathcal G_n|}\\) inflation and this factor is not part of \\(b_{nm}\\).  This conservative finite-sample result makes no claim that the frozen leave-one-cell-out multiplier critical value is asymptotically exact.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "G",
      "g",
      "P",
      "tauhat",
      "tau",
      "alpha",
      "B",
      "n",
      "m",
      "q",
      "b"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
